2. Page Inventory
2.1 Page 1 — Champion Onboarding (Universal)
Audience: All institution champions. Sent by PMs: Always.


Page structure


Page 1 is built from seven sections, each containing one custom HTML embed or one Google Form embed:


Block 1 — Hero header Branded hero banner with headline and intro copy. Sets context for the champion.


Block 2 — Role cards Explains the champion role: what it involves, who uses the Explorer, and how the onboarding process works.


Block 3 — Your Explorer instance Two-column card layout. Left card: what Digital Science sets up. Right card: what we need from the champion (access configuration and optional co-branding). Neutral info treatment, no action-required pill.


Block 4 — Setting up access Three-column card layout for the three access methods (SSO, IP Range, Individual Accounts). Each card covers how the method works, best-fit scenarios, and what the champion needs to provide. Proxy access is presented as a callout below the cards rather than a fourth peer option, as proxy is an add-on to IP range access rather than a standalone method. A second callout handles the "not sure" case.


Block 5 — Access setup form (embedded Google Form) Primary intake form. Captures all details needed to configure access. Branches by access method after Q5. See Section 3.1 for the full question inventory.


Block 6 — Getting your research tracked Two-column card layout explaining how Altmetric tracking works and what identifiers are supported. Includes a link to the Altmetric support KB tracking category. Callout for champions whose contract includes a data integration.


Block 7 — Next steps Four numbered steps covering the journey from form submission to user rollout, including the orientation session note (use cases to support@altmetric.com, minimum one week notice). Contact card with support@altmetric.com.


