2.2 Page 2 — Data Integrations (Optional)
Audience: Champions whose contract includes a data integration (Elements, Pure, OAI-PMH, or CSV). Sent by PMs: Only when a data integration is in scope. Not sent universally.


Page structure


Block 1 — Intro Explains why integrations exist: Altmetric tracks attention globally but does not know which outputs belong to the institution. Two-column cards: what a data integration does, and how to identify which type applies.


Block 2 — Tabbed integration type cards Four tabs: Symplectic Elements, Pure, OAI-PMH, CSV. Champion selects the tab matching their contract. Each tab covers what the integration is, who needs to be involved, what to provide, caveats (self-hosted Elements config, Pure firewall, Haplo department limitation), and a link to the relevant implementation documentation.


Documentation links by tab:


* Elements: https://docs.altmetric.com/implementation/populating-data/#symplectic-elements
* Pure: https://docs.altmetric.com/implementation/populating-data/#pure
* OAI-PMH: https://docs.altmetric.com/implementation/populating-data/#harvesting-from-your-repository-oai-pmh-feed
* CSV: https://docs.altmetric.com/implementation/populating-data/#send-your-publications-data-via-csv-spreadsheet


Block 3 — Integration intake form (embedded Google Form) Single branching form. Branches by integration type after Q1 (type selection). Credentials are never collected in the form — champions are directed to share via Privnote to support@altmetric.com. See Section 3.2 for the full question inventory.


Block 4 — Getting started callout Confirms that the Implementation Manager will be in touch to kick off the process. Notes that Elements, Pure, and OAI-PMH integrations run on staging first with a preview shared for approval. Contact: support@altmetric.com.


