2.3 Page 3 — Badges (Optional)
Audience: Champions whose contract includes Altmetric Badges. Sent by PMs: Only when badges are in scope. Not sent universally.


Page structure


Block 1 — Badges intro Explains what badges are, how they update automatically, and that embedding is a client action requiring the champion's web or repository team. Link to badge documentation: https://docs.altmetric.com/badges/.


Block 2 — Badge variant cards Three-column layout. Order: Regular (unlocked), Customised, Limited (locked). Each card covers what the variant shows and what the champion needs to provide. Limited is presented last as it is infrequently sold. Callout at bottom handles the "not sure" case and confirms the default.


Block 3 — Badges intake form (embedded Google Form) Branches by badge variant. Regular and Limited collect domain(s) and optional web/repository contact. Customised adds logo email confirmation and background colour hex code. See Section 3.3 for the full question inventory.


Block 4 — What happens next Four steps: we configure, we share badge documentation, champion's team embeds the code, we verify. Notes that customised badges involve a dev team step and may take one to two weeks. Contact: support@altmetric.com.


