5. Working With the Page Code
5.1 How to access the HTML for any block
1. Open the Edit URL for the relevant page (listed in Section 2 once confirmed).
2. Click on any content block to select it.
3. Click the pencil (edit) icon — for custom HTML blocks this opens the embed editor showing the raw HTML.
4. Select all and copy.


Each page has multiple separate embed blocks. Open each one individually. Block boundaries correspond to the section descriptions in Section 2.
5.2 Making changes with Claude
1. Open a Claude chat (claude.ai) in the Altmetric onboarding project.
2. Paste in the HTML for the block you want to change.
3. Describe what you want to update.
4. Claude will return the updated HTML. Copy and paste it back into the Google Sites embed editor.
5. Click Done, then Publish in Google Sites to make the change live.
5.3 Tips
* Change one block at a time rather than pasting all blocks into a single Claude message.
* If making the same change across multiple pages (e.g. a support email update), do each block separately and check before moving on.
* The iframe background fix must be present on every block: html { background: #2A265A; } and body { display: table; width: 100%; }. Do not remove these.
* Always preview the page in Google Sites before publishing.


